    <ImplementationPlan>
      <T-001>
        <Title>kafedra-flow-intake: define immutable gradebook states and immediate destination</Title>
        <DependsOn></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The primary flow is upload source, preserve documentId and version, analyze, correct ambiguity, import and open the exact current group-period summary without a redundant confirmation screen.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Failures preserve the source and operator selections; a failed row, cell or later version does not block valid facts or replace the previous current import.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --test tests/academic-performance.test.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-001>
      <T-002>
        <Title>kafedra-data: integrate schema 31, provenance, lifecycle, totals and recovery</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-001 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Migration 031 is the next additive immutable migration and stores groups, periods, students, memberships, disciplines, imports, bindings, records and issues with source locators.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Current, superseded, archived and restored states are idempotent; academic tables participate in logical digest, backup and restore.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Selected-current-group totals are calculated from grade records with a weighted numeric-only average and are not stored as a second truth.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --test tests/academic-performance-migration.test.mjs tests/academic-performance-backup.test.mjs tests/academic-performance-period-totals.test.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-002>
      <T-003>
        <Title>kafedra-design: deliver stable desktop and mobile academic hierarchy</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-001 /><T-002 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Desktop shows academic year, semester and group navigation beside the selected summary; mobile presents the same flow as sequential sections without horizontal dependency.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>One primary upload/import path, visible source bindings, calm table hierarchy, empty/loading/partial/error states and evidence drill-down remain stable regardless of usage statistics.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>The Action Center gains a fixed Учебный процесс group without moving global controls or changing the fixed recommendation geometry.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --check tests/browser/academic-performance.spec.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-003>
      <T-004>
        <Title>kafedra-motion: keep disclosure restrained and provide true reduced-motion</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-003 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Only short disclosure transitions assist orientation; importing, totals, table updates and evidence remain understandable in static frames.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>prefers-reduced-motion computes zero transition duration and introduces no spatial animation on desktop or mobile.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --check tests/browser/academic-performance.spec.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-004>
      <T-005>
        <Title>kafedra-feature: integrate API, section, Action Center and exports end to end</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-002 /><T-003 /><T-004 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The current application router and ux-next load the academic module without replacing newer Action Center, documents, plans, meetings, science or release code.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>academic.import launches the existing academic import form, is allowlisted and rank-only, and records preference only after successful explicit launch.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>CSV, JSON and sources exports include per-group detail and selected-group totals while preserving exact source navigation.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --test tests/academic-performance-wiring.test.mjs tests/action-center-registry.test.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-005>
      <T-006>
        <Title>kafedra-design-audit: independently verify clarity, evidence and responsive parity</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-005 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The implemented interface has no blocker or major finding for desktop, mobile, keyboard, source visibility, partial success, preserved input or reduced-motion.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-006>
      <T-007>
        <Title>kafedra-tests: prove normalization, lifecycle, ACL, totals and complete browser flows</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-006 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Unit and integration tests cover grade aliases, blanks, unknowns, columns after Z, cell/manual metadata, current replacement, failed replacement, archive/restore, ACL, idempotency, totals and all exports.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Playwright covers the Action Center entry and direct navigation, desktop, mobile, selected groups, evidence, exports, retry and true zero-duration reduced motion.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm test</Command><Command>node --check tests/browser/academic-performance.spec.mjs</Command><Command>node --check tests/browser/action-center.spec.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-007>
      <T-008>
        <Title>kafedra-release: publish verified 0.4.0 offline release candidate</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-007 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>VERSION, package manifests, release markers and notes agree on 0.4.0; schema documentation and acceptance agree on 31.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Exact-head GRACE, project, release, database, browser and full-offline checks pass; post-merge publisher creates immutable release assets and checksums without moving an old tag.</Criterion>
